WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.530
My robot walked round the football

2
00:00:02.530 --> 00:00:04.690
pitch with sixteen cards.

3
00:00:05.490 --> 00:00:08.710
Forward, forward, forward, turn.

4
00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:10.740
Again and again!

5
00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:13.880
There must be a shorter way.

6
00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:17.560
Today: loops, the shorter way.

7
00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:19.490
Look at the cards.

8
00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:22.940
Forward three times, then turn.

9
00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:25.480
The same four cards come

10
00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:27.120
again, four times.

11
00:00:27.770 --> 00:00:29.790
Steps that repeat make a pattern.

12
00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:32.970
A loop tells the robot to repeat.

13
00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:35.540
Instead of laying the same card

14
00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:38.120
again and again, you lay it once

15
00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:39.860
and say how many times.

16
00:00:40.490 --> 00:00:42.050
Forward, three times.

17
00:00:43.330 --> 00:00:45.130
Loops make programs shorter.

18
00:00:45.850 --> 00:00:47.670
They are easier to read.

19
00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:49.870
And if you want the robot to go

20
00:00:49.870 --> 00:00:52.270
further, you change just one number.

21
00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:54.600
You know loops already.

22
00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:57.580
A clapping game repeats the same claps.

23
00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:00.110
A song repeats its chorus.

24
00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:02.520
Skipping a rope is a loop:

25
00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:04.820
jump, again and again.

26
00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:06.540
Quick check!

27
00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:09.020
The robot has one card:

28
00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:11.380
forward, four times.

29
00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:13.670
How many squares does it move?

30
00:01:14.920 --> 00:01:15.680
Four squares.

31
00:01:16.660 --> 00:01:19.620
One card, but it repeats four times.

32
00:01:20.260 --> 00:01:21.740
In the app, a card can

33
00:01:21.740 --> 00:01:23.520
repeat up to four times.

34
00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:27.880
In the app, open Program a robot.

35
00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:30.900
Tap a card in your program to repeat it.

36
00:01:31.460 --> 00:01:32.940
Can you win three stars,

37
00:01:33.320 --> 00:01:34.380
with the fewest cards?

38
00:01:35.780 --> 00:01:36.540
Your turn.

39
00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:39.180
Which program is shorter, but walks

40
00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:41.580
the same way: forward, forward,

41
00:01:41.860 --> 00:01:44.380
forward, or forward, three times?

42
00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:47.160
Forward, three times.

43
00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:49.400
Remember: steps that

44
00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:50.860
repeat make a pattern.

45
00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:53.260
A loop repeats them for you.

46
00:01:53.860 --> 00:01:55.600
Loops make programs shorter

47
00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:57.300
and easier to change.

48
00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:00.480
Try it yourself: make up a

49
00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:01.420
dance with a loop.

50
00:02:02.050 --> 00:02:04.550
Write it on paper, like step,

51
00:02:05.010 --> 00:02:07.190
step, clap, four times.

52
00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:09.040
Teach it to someone at home,

53
00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:10.880
using only your paper!
